<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Mathematical Derivations</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide detailed mathematical derivations for two key components of margin loss: (1) how LogSumExp (LSE) function approximates the maximum function, and (2) the complete derivation steps of our margin loss formulation based on LSE.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>LSE Approximation of Maximum Function</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The LogSumExp function is defined as:</p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LSE(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})=\log(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp(x_{i}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LSE(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})=\log(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp(x_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">First, we prove that LSE provides an upper bound for the maximum function. For any <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E11X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle LSE(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle LSE(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{n}\exp(x_{j})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{n}\exp(x_{j})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E11Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\log(\exp(x_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\log(\exp(x_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E11Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since this holds for all <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LSE(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})\geq\max(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LSE(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})\geq\max(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}=\max(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}=\max(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. We can rewrite LSE as:</p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle LSE(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})=\log\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp(x_{i})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle LSE(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})=\log\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp(x_{i})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E13Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(\exp(x^{*})\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp(x_{i}-x^{*})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(\exp(x^{*})\sum_{i=1}^{n}\exp(x_{i}-x^{*})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E13Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x^{*}+\quad\log\left(1+\sum_{i:x_{i}\neq x^{*}}\exp(x_{i}-x^{*})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x^{*}+\quad\log\left(1+\sum_{i:x_{i}\neq x^{*}}\exp(x_{i}-x^{*})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}-x^{*}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}-x^{*}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> (with equality only when <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}=x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}=x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>), and typically <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}-x^{*}\ll 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}-x^{*}\ll 0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\neq x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\neq x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(x_{i}-x^{*})\rightarrow 0\text{ when }x_{i}-x^{*}\ll 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> when </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(x_{i}-x^{*})\rightarrow 0\text{ when }x_{i}-x^{*}\ll 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore:</p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log(1+\sum_{i:x_{i}\neq x^{*}}\exp(x_{i}-x^{*}))\rightarrow 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1+\sum_{i:x_{i}\neq x^{*}}\exp(x_{i}-x^{*}))\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This yields our final approximation:</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LSE(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})\approx x^{*}=\max(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LSE(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})\approx x^{*}=\max(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The approximation becomes more accurate as the differences between the maximum value and other values increase.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Derivation of Margin Loss</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Starting from the initial margin loss formulation:</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{Margin}}\approx\left[LSE\left(\gamma\left(s_{n}\right)\right)-\left(-LSE\left(-\gamma\left(s_{p}\right)\right)\right)\right]_{+}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>Margin</mtext></msub><mo>≈</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{Margin}}\approx\left[LSE\left(\gamma\left(s_{n}\right)\right)-\left(-LSE\left(-\gamma\left(s_{p}\right)\right)\right)\right]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We can expand this expression:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[LSE\left(\gamma\left(s_{n}\right)\right)-\left(-NLSE\left(\gamma\left(s_{p}\right)\right)\right)\right]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[LSE\left(\gamma\left(s_{n}\right)\right)-\left(-NLSE\left(\gamma\left(s_{p}\right)\right)\right)\right]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\log\sum_{j=1}^{L}\exp\left(\gamma\left(s_{n}^{j}\right)\right)+\log\sum_{i=1}^{K}\exp\left(\gamma\left(-s_{p}^{i}\right)\right)\right]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mi>exp</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup><mi>exp</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\log\sum_{j=1}^{L}\exp\left(\gamma\left(s_{n}^{j}\right)\right)+\log\sum_{i=1}^{K}\exp\left(\gamma\left(-s_{p}^{i}\right)\right)\right]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E18Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{L}\exp\left(\gamma\left(s_{n}^{j}\right)\right)\sum_{i=1}^{K}\exp\left(\gamma\left(-s_{p}^{i}\right)\right)\right)\right]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\log\left(\sum_{j=1}^{L}\exp\left(\gamma\left(s_{n}^{j}\right)\right)\sum_{i=1}^{K}\exp\left(\gamma\left(-s_{p}^{i}\right)\right)\right)\right]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E18Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\log\sum_{i=1}^{K}\sum_{j=1}^{L}\exp\left(\gamma\left(s_{n}^{j}-s_{p}^{i}\right)\right)\right]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mi>exp</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\log\sum_{i=1}^{K}\sum_{j=1}^{L}\exp\left(\gamma\left(s_{n}^{j}-s_{p}^{i}\right)\right)\right]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, using the softplus function to smooth the ReLU operation:</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{\text{Margin}}\approx\log\left[1+\sum_{i=1}^{K}\sum_{j=1}^{L}\exp\left(\gamma\left(s_{n}^{j}-s_{p}^{i}\right)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>Margin</mtext></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{\text{Margin}}\approx\log\left[1+\sum_{i=1}^{K}\sum_{j=1}^{L}\exp\left(\gamma\left(s_{n}^{j}-s_{p}^{i}\right)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This completes the derivation of our margin loss formulation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
